## 3. Dual-Axis Configuration Rules (The "Fix")

The previous failure stemmed from missing `yAxisId` on `<YAxis>` components and/or missing `yAxisId` on `<Bar>`/`<Line>` series, causing Recharts to default everything to the first axis.

### Mandatory Binding Matrix

| Element | Prop | Required Value |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `<YAxis>` (Left) | `yAxisId` | `"revenue"` |
| `<YAxis>` (Left) | `orientation` | `"left"` |
| `<YAxis>` (Right) | `yAxisId` | `"orders"` |
| `<YAxis>` (Right) | `orientation` | `"right"` |
| `<Bar>` | `yAxisId` | `"revenue"` |
| `<Bar>` | `dataKey` | `"revenue"` |
| `<Line>` | `yAxisId` | `"orders"` |
| `<Line>` | `dataKey` | `"orders"` |

### Independent Scaling Logic
1.  **Do not** set `domain` prop on `<YAxis>`. Allow Recharts `auto` calculation (default) per axis.
2.  **Do not** use `syncId` on axes.
3.  **Tick Formatter**: Revenue axis uses currency (`$`, `k`/`M` suffix). Orders axis uses integer/number formatting (`#`, `k` suffix).
4.  **Tooltip**: Must be shared (`<Tooltip shared />`) but format values per series using `formatter` prop on `<Tooltip>` or custom `labelFormatter`/`formatter` on series. **Preferred**: Custom `Tooltip` content or `formatter` on Tooltip receiving `(value, name, props)` where `props.payload[0].dataKey` identifies the axis.

